cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite its version and the specific model assumptions. Numerical verification is not biological validation."
title: "Encounter Check"
type: software
version: 0.2.0-alpha
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/dataRichinsightPoor/encounter-check"
url: "https://datarichinsightpoor.github.io/encounter-check/"
authors:
  - name: "Data-Rich, Insight-Poor"
abstract: "A research-use mass-action model of effector-target killing in a well. It tests when the effector-to-target ratio describes a co-culture and when cell density does, compares settled and bulk contact geometries, checks whether lysis can distinguish contact rate from kill probability, and designs density-resolving plates. An optional bispecific bridge adds equilibrium drug binding with depletion, so dose and density interact. Scenarios are synthetic and imply no statistical coverage, power, or therapeutic prediction."
